  "description": "The proposed parklet will be completed by Meristem Design on behalf of the Harley Street Business Improvement District. The structure is a public parklet replacing two existing car parking spaces, opposite the library. The design proposes placement of a parklet (which is not fixed to\nthe ground) with elements of seating, planting and community engagement. The seating consists of different tiered seating for all ages, benches and rest zones to stand while engaging with the planting or community activities. The community engagement items include a public book swap cabinet, interactive kids play wall, book cover panels, a mock SuDS planter for members of the community to learn from, bug hotels, information boards, and a chess board table. The planting will be present in square steel planters powder coated green, and in planters attached to trellis for ivy/jasmine climbers, which will have a solar panel frame. The solar panels attached to the trellis will be south facing to maximise solar gain. They will power an air quality sensor and foot traffic sensors in the parklet, to monitor quality and use. This design aims to create a nature parklet for pedestrians and the local community to use as a third degree space, for rest, relaxation and\nconnection to nature. It also encourages users to learn about sustainable construction principles, such as sustainable drainage systems and solar panels. Furthermore, it will create a positive experience for the local community.",
